course: dictionary
lesson: 10851
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word vest can mean different things, and the words around it show you which one. Ask yourself what the vest is doing and where it is. «Hard hats protect heads from falling things, and hi-vis vests make workers easy to see.» The clue is "make workers easy to see", so this vest is a bright safety top.
explain: The same word can name different clothes in different places. In the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, a vest is underwear worn under a shirt. In the USA and Canada, a vest is a sleeveless jacket worn over a shirt, which the UK calls a waistcoat. If a friend talks about a vest, check which place they mean.
explain: Be careful with words from other languages. «Some clothes words are traps for English speakers: une veste is a jacket, not a vest.» A French veste has sleeves, so it is not a vest in English. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A vest is a sleeveless top, so it has no sleeves at all.
fact: «Vest» means underwear worn under a shirt in the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand.
fact: «Vest» means a sleeveless jacket worn over a shirt in the USA and Canada.
fact: «Hi-vis» means high visibility, so a «hi-vis vest» is bright and easy to see.
fact: A «steward» is a helper who often wears a bright vest at an event.
exercise: «Hard hats protect heads, and hi-vis vests make workers easy to see.» What is a hi-vis vest for? | *To make workers easy to see | To keep workers warm under a shirt | To protect the head from falling things | To show which team you are on
exercise: «A vest has no sleeves at all, so vests add nothing to the number of sleeves.» How many sleeves does a vest have? | Two | One | *None | Four
exercise: «Some clothes words are traps for English speakers: une veste is a jacket, not a vest.» What does une veste mean in English? | Trainers | A vest | A dress | *A jacket
test: In the USA, Maya wears a sleeveless top over her shirt and calls it a vest. What is it? | A pair of trainers | A piece of underwear worn under a shirt | *A sleeveless jacket worn over a shirt | A bright top for a boat
test: «If you are lost in a crowd, ask a police officer or a steward (a helper in a bright vest at the event).» Who is a steward? | A police officer on a horse | A lost child looking for their family | *A helper in a bright vest at the event | A shop owner
exam: In a shop in the UK, Tom asks for a vest to wear under his shirt. What does he want? | A sleeveless jacket to wear over his shirt | A dress | A life vest for a boat | *A piece of underwear worn under a shirt
